    size: 3x3, fully filled (no background pixels)
    colors: exactly 2 distinct non-bg non-marker colors [observed always 1 and 8]
    color_split: 3-6 pixels of one color, remainder of the other
    asymmetry: must NOT be invariant under any rot90 k=1,2,3
    position: centered with margins >=3 on all sides
  markers:
    count: 4 singleton pixels, all same color, distinct from bg and sprite colors [observed always 4/yellow]
    L-group: 3 markers forming an L at 3 corners of a 2x2 square centered 1 cell diag-outside the dst sprite corner; the 4th square corner is the dst sprite corner itself
    singleton: 1 marker at the cell 1 diag-outside the src sprite corner
    src != dst corner; rotation steps 1-3 (no identity) [observed]
  output:
    sprite rotated in-place by the unique quarter-turn mapping src corner to dst corner
    all 4 input markers removed
    1 marker pixel placed at the center of the L-group's 2x2 square
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - Pick grid size 10-12 x 10-11
    - Choose 3 distinct non-bg colors for sprite_c1, sprite_c2, marker_color
