    5. Fill all remaining cells randomly from {black, red, green, yellow, orange}
       with approximate proportions black~30%, red~22%, green~20%, yellow~10%, orange~15%.
    6. Verify no spurious green matches exist beyond the intended K copies (reject if so).
       To reduce rejection, place copies first, then fill noise, then re-check.
    7. Build input by recoloring the K copy positions from teal back to green.
       Output has all copies in teal; input has them in green.
